// Wildcard re-export builds a "prelude".  `pub use foo::*;` lifts every
// public item of a child module up into its parent, so one `use parent::*;`
// downstream pulls in the whole tree without listing names one at a time.
//
// `prelude` (examples/prelude/mod.exl) re-exports its `greetings` and
// `farewells` submodules.  `main` imports `prelude::*` and calls the
// functions unqualified — each arrived through two hops of re-export.
//
// Re-export is file-modules only; an inline `mod { ... }` block re-exports
// per name (see examples/modules).

use prelude::*;

fn main() {
    hello();                                  // from prelude::greetings
    goodbye();                                // from prelude::farewells
}
